            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 26 changed paths. The change is a requested retirement (follow-up F1) of the prespec verbs and the engine/prespec package. It only deletes code, routes, help text, manifest rows and tests, plus comment and doc edits. It adds no new input handling, no secrets and no dependencies.",
              "The deleted code read JSON from stdin and wrote JSON to stdout, so removing it shrinks the attack surface. The engine now rejects the prespec subcommand as unknown, and a test pins that behavior (engine/cmd/dispatch_routes_test.go:28-29).",
              "The wrapper script no longer routes prespec (bin/labdrian-overlay) and no longer defines cmd_prespec (bin/lib/engine_verbs.sh). The test in engine/skills/clarify_request_test.go confirms no remaining route, definition or help entry. The task log (odd/tasks/clarify-request.md) says only engine/cmd imported engine/prespec, so no other consumer is visible as broken. That claim comes from the log, not from the diff itself.",
              "No data loss or authorization impact is reachable. Stale installed prespec-malandra copies are noted as pending the owner and are outside this change."
